#
# minja carries b70 patches (spec 18d; every one marked "b70 patch (spec 18d)" in the source,
# each tested against Jinja2 by tests/tokenizer/minja_ext_test.cc). The sha256s above are the
# patched minja.hpp and chat-template.hpp; upstream at the pin they were
#   55df85289038d54566ac40903617725e82a9e07e60a21b38dc6de65f7b7e10b8 (minja.hpp)
#   87db93c98fd215b70b6f8908f55015a696cd92564dd4fced19bb11f103d475d4 (chat-template.hpp)
# The patches make K2-Horizon's chat template render as transformers' Jinja does:
#   minja.hpp          Jinja's Undefined apart from None (`{"default": null}` is defined);
#                      `is [not] sameas <value>`; str.split() with no separator (Unicode
#                      whitespace); the `replace` filter; the `dict` global; attribute getters
#                      whose all-digit parts index (rejectattr('0', ...) on `| items` pairs);
#                      an empty mapping is falsy; the lower-case `none` literal.
#   chat-template.hpp  the tool-call capability probe also accepts ">argument_needle<" (an
#                      argument name between tags), so K2's tool-call history is rendered by
#                      its template instead of being polyfilled into JSON content.
#                      b70 patch (spec 23e): and `name="argument_needle"` (an argument name as a
#                      double-quoted attribute - Muse-Glimmer's ATEM <atem:parameter name="...">),
#                      for the same reason (tests/tokenizer/minja_ext_test.cc's
#                      tool_call_probe_attribute case).
#                      b70 patch (spec 24e): and `(argument_needle=` (a pythonic keyword argument opening the call's
#                      parentheses - LFM2.5's `name(k='v')`), for the same reason; and the arguments rewrite that stays
#                      on when arguments must be an object leaves a call without a "function" object or without
#                      "arguments" alone (upstream threw; the LFM2.5 template reads them with .get() and renders `name()`).
#                      Tested by minja_ext_test's tool_call_probe_pythonic case.
#   minja.hpp          b70 patches (spec 24e), each against Jinja2 3.1.6 in minja_ext_cases.json (in_falsy, float_str,
#                      float_tojson): `x in [..]` is plain equality (upstream skipped falsy items: `'' in ['']` was false,
#                      which made LFM2.5's `(args | trim) not in ["", "{}", "null"]` raise on an empty arguments string);
#                      str(float) / `{{ float }}` / a float inside tojson print as Python's repr (1.0, 1e-07, 1e+20; upstream
#                      std::to_string wrote 1.000000, 0.000000, and nlohmann wrote 1e+15 for Python's 1000000000000000.0).
#                      `==` on a primitive (None included) is false against an array / object / callable (upstream: `[1] in [none]`
#                      was true; in_falsy's last five cases).
# The Qwen3.8 / Agnes template tests are unchanged by them (byte-identical renders).
